Apply the same workaround as archives/s/sdl_image/1.2.12 (0001-configure.patch)
and archives/b/ballandpaddle/0.8.1 (0001-configure-umask.patch): OHOS HMDFS does
not honour chmod, so a 0700 temporary directory created by mktemp -d is not
writable by the build process. configure then prints success but never writes a
Makefile, or later dies on './confXXXXXX/subs-1.sed: Permission denied'.

Relax the umask used for configure's own temporary directory from 077 to 022.
Purely a portability fix; no behaviour change on other systems.

Both occurrences live inside the same 12-line block, so they are kept in a single
hunk: Conan applies these patches with patch_ng, which validates hunks by walking
the file once and cannot re-synchronise when a hunk starts before the previous
one ends (it raises IndexError instead of applying the patch).

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -5651,12 +5651,12 @@
 # Create a (secure) tmp directory for tmp files.

 {
-  tmp=`(umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
+  tmp=`(umask 022 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
   test -d "$tmp"
 }  ||
 {
   tmp=./conf$$-$RANDOM
-  (umask 077 && mkdir "$tmp")
+  (umask 022 && mkdir "$tmp")
 } || as_fn_error $? "cannot create a temporary directory in ." "$LINENO" 5
 ac_tmp=$tmp

